===============================================================================
NOTICE — third-party material and scope of the grant above
===============================================================================

This is a kernel-mode driver, and like essentially every PortCls audio driver
it is structured after Microsoft's own sample drivers. The MIT grant above
covers the original work in this repository. It does not, and cannot, relicense
the material described below.

1. Microsoft WDK 7600 sample drivers
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Portions of the driver's structure — the adapter/subdevice registration
   pattern, the WaveCyclic miniport and stream skeleton, the DMA channel
   abstraction, and the topology miniport — derive from the "ac97", "msvad"
   and "toaster" sample drivers distributed with the Windows Driver Kit
   7600.16385.1. The INF's legacy wave-mapper registration
   (AssociatedFilters, Drivers\SubClasses and the wdmaud.drv sub-driver
   entries) is modelled closely on msvad.inf, and the [DDInstall.HW] security
   placement follows the pattern used by toastco.inf and the other WDK
   samples.

   That sample code remains Microsoft's, under whatever terms accompanied
   your copy of the WDK. Using the samples as the basis for a driver is their
   documented purpose; redistributing them as if they were MIT-licensed is not
   something this file attempts to do.

2. Microsoft-supplied binaries referenced but NOT distributed here
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The INF registers ksthunk.sys as an upper filter on the MEDIA device class.
   ksthunk.sys is a component of Windows XP x64 itself and is NOT included in
   or copied by this package — it is already present on every XP x64 install.
   Microsoft's UAA bus driver (KB888111) is a prerequisite and is likewise not
   included; obtain it from Microsoft.

3. Material deliberately excluded from this repository
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------
   No code from IDT's proprietary stwrt64.sys driver is present in this
   repository in any form, neither source nor disassembly nor decompiled
   output. The driver here was written against the WDK, the Intel High
   Definition Audio specification, and the codec's own responses.

   The Linux kernel's sound/pci/hda sources were consulted as a behavioural
   reference for the SigmaTel/IDT codec family. Those files are GPL-2.0 and
   are NOT included here; no code was copied from them.

4. No warranty, emphatically
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Read the all-caps paragraph above and take it seriously. This is an
   unsigned kernel-mode driver for an operating system that left support in
   2015, written for one specific machine. A defective kernel driver can
   bluescreen a system or, in principle, damage data. It is offered because it
   works on the hardware it was built for and may help someone with the same
   problem. Nothing more is promised.
